  "graph": {
    "note": "Conformance fixtures for the intent-graph read model (ADR-0014, schema/intent-graph.schema.json). Unlike the catalog vectors these pin STRUCTURE, not ETags: the graph is not a synced wire artifact in v1. Both producers — the in-process local learner and the Ratel Cloud builder — MUST emit graphs that validate, and every consumer MUST reject the `invalid` set.",
    "consumerRules": [
      "An edge naming a capability absent from the consumer's registry MUST be dropped, never ranked — the catalog may have changed since the graph was grown.",
      "`centroid` MAY be absent; a consumer without an embedder matches lexically over `members`, and one with an embedder MAY derive a centroid from `members`.",
      "A consumer MUST NOT mix centroids produced by different embedding models; on a model change, discard the centroids and re-derive from `members`.",
      "`label` and `terms` are display-only. Retrieval results MUST be identical whatever they contain.",
      "Edge weights are observation COUNTS, and absolute magnitudes are never compared against BM25 or cosine scores. They are not, on their own, the order to serve: a consumer SHOULD down-weight a capability that appears across many clusters, because one that answers every intent identifies none of them. Ratel scales each edge by 1 + ln(clusters / clusters naming that capability), counted over the raw edge maps of every cluster \u2014 not over the edges that survive a consumer's own catalog filter, which would make the order depend on which catalog is attached rather than on the graph.",
      "`cluster_policy` MAY be absent, meaning the built-in defaults. It is PROVENANCE: it records the similarity and coverage the graph's existing boundaries were drawn under, not what a consumer should cluster at next. A consumer clustering at different values MUST NOT assume the existing boundaries match them \u2014 boundaries are never redrawn in place.",
      "`cohesion` MAY be absent, meaning 1.0. A consumer that matches on `centroid` without per-member vectors SHOULD scale the similarity it requires by it: a normalized centroid hides how far apart its members are, so a cluster that drifted apart otherwise reads as tight and keeps absorbing.",
      "`vector_n` is provenance for learning only \u2014 it weights the next fold into `centroid`. Retrieval results MUST be identical whatever it contains.",
      "`seeded_support` is provenance only — it records how many of `support` came from a seeding pass rather than live traffic. Retrieval results MUST be identical whatever it contains.",
      "`surfaced_tools` and `surfaced_skills` are provenance only — it counts how many of a cluster's searches put each capability in front of the caller, so a consumer can tell a capability that is shown constantly and rarely used from one shown rarely and always used. A consumer MUST NOT let it affect ranking, and MUST NOT treat an id present in an impression map but absent from the matching edge map as an edge: what retrieval returned is not evidence, only what was invoked is. The two maps exist because tool and skill ids are different id spaces: an id in one MUST NOT be read against the other."
    ],
